From 851508db4e3cc9b6e1194e461ac950bdcd15dc69 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stlalpha <spaceman@themcbros.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Oct 2025 11:57:43 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Replace POSIX semaphores with condition variables to remove
 2GB buffer limit

This change removes the buffer size limitation that was previously capped
at sysconf(_SC_SEM_VALUE_MAX) * Blocksize (typically ~2GB) due to POSIX
semaphores using 32-bit integer counters.

Implementation:
- Replaced sem_t Dev2Buf and Buf2Dev with 64-bit counters (FreeBlocks, FullBlocks)
- Added pthread mutexes and condition variables for synchronization
- Created counter_init(), counter_wait(), counter_post(), and counter_getvalue() helper functions
- Updated all semaphore operations throughout codebase to use new counter primitives
- Removed maxSemValue() limitation checks from settings validation

Benefits:
- Buffer size now only limited by available system memory
- Enables buffers larger than 2GB on systems with sufficient RAM
- Maintains thread-safe synchronization using mutex-protected 64-bit counters

Files modified:
- globals.h/c: Defined new sync primitives and counters
- common.h/c: Implemented counter operation functions
- mbuffer.c: Replaced all semaphore operations in main and output threads
- input.c: Replaced all semaphore operations in input thread
- settings.c: Removed semaphore limit validation
- README: Updated documentation to reflect removed limitation
